Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0035 (touches the DSpark
model, its Markov cache ops, spec_decode/dspark/speculator.py, spec_decode/depth_policy.py and the V2 model runner).
VLLM_DSPARK_CONF_FEAT_HEAD=<feat_head.npz> (default unset; needs the local draft argmax and VLLM_DSPARK_MARKOV_FUSED=1):
the speculator also computes, per draft position i, sigmoid(w[i,0] + w[i,1] z_i + w[i,2] m_i + w[i,3] logit(p1_i)) over
the confidence head's logit z_i, the draft's (top-1 - top-2) logit margin m_i and its top-1 probability p1_i over the
whole vocabulary (w [k, 4] from scripts/dspark/fit_draft_features.py --export on a fixed:k round log with patch 0034's
features), and the depth policy's conf rule reads these under VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_POLICY=conf+feat (the head's own
confidences stay in draft_token_confidence_probs and the round log). The fused Markov argmax (0031) keeps each shard's
second-largest value and logsumexp next to its (max, index) pair in the same two launches
(MarkovBiasCache.argmax_record), the all-gather carries four floats a row instead of two, and the features come from
the gathered records inside the captured draft step; the (max, index) columns are argmax_pair's bit for bit, so the
drafts do not move, and only the verify depth reads the confidences, so greedy text does not change either.
VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_FILE is now also read at the first verify step after a request starts, so "conf:<ms,...>" and
"conf+feat:<ms,...>" can alternate request by request in one serve (an A/B without boot-to-boot noise).
Why: on our panel (11,357 fixed:5 rounds, 30 prompts a domain) the head + draft features replay +1.2% overall and +1.6% on set b's prose
reply over the head alone; a 5,376-wide refit of the head itself gains +0.2-0.3% (Oct 21).
Test: patches/tests/test_dspark_conf_feat_head.py (serve image).

